invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_vector.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: lane 1 starts from the accumulator as lane 0 does, so the value
  of every block before the update counts twice, once times each lane's
  powers. Its first update comes out right only when the accumulator is
  0, which is exactly when a message's first update reaches the path, so
  only an update after earlier blocks shows the fault.
  bin/poly1305_equiv_test cuts every message into two or three updates
  and calls poly1305_vector_blocks after one to four earlier blocks.

--- old
    h[0] = words_of(p->h[0], 0);
--- new
    h[0] = words_of(p->h[0], p->h[0]);
